      "text_raw": "In the same way, series feed-\nback, shown here at the\ninput of an amplifier, causes\nthe input voltage to in-\ncrease. This input voltage\nv is the total voltage from\nIN\ngate to ground. It is the sum\nof the actual transistor v\nGS\nand the voltage v across the\nS\nfeedback resistor R .\nS\nThe total input voltage\nwill therefore be larger than\nwithout feedback. As a\nresult, the ratio v /i ,\nIN IN\nwhich is the input resistance\nR , will increase by the\nIN\namount of loop gain real-\nized by the feedback loop.",
      "text": "In the same way, series feedback, shown here at the input of an amplifier, causes the input voltage to increase. This input voltage v is the total voltage from IN gate to ground. It is the sum of the actual transistor v GS and the voltage v across the S feedback resistor R . S The total input voltage will therefore be larger than without feedback. As a result, the ratio v /i , IN IN which is the input resistance R , will increase by the IN amount of loop gain realized by the feedback loop."
